(    Help For RazzledazzleX)Tj
0 -2.4 TD
(      Introduction)Tj
T*
(Welcome to the network RazzledazzleX server. RazzledazzleX is an)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(implementation of the tournament version of Razzledazzle.)Tj
0 -2.4 TD
(Razzledazzle is \(c\) 2005 Donald Green and Family Games. Check out his)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(other games on the server: Octi <octi.html> \(Octi3base <octi3base.html>\,)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(OctiLite <octilite.html>\), Hexi <hexi.html> \(Hexi3base)Tj
T*
(<hexi3base.html>\), and Razzledazzle <razzledazzle.html>.)Tj
0 -2.4 TD
(The rules of Razzledazzle <#rules> are below. Commands <commands.html>)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(are the same for all pbmserv games.)Tj
0 -3.6 TD
(      Move Notation)Tj
0 -2.4 TD
(Moves are of the form <from>-<to> where from and to are specified as)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(file and rank coordinates. Files run from a to g and ranks run from 1 to\)Tj
T*
(8. Passing the ball is indicated in the same fashion, possibly with)Tj
T*
(additional -<to> squares tacked on the end.)Tj
0 -3.6 TD
(      Rules for Razzledazzle)Tj
0 -3.6 TD
(      Object of the game:)Tj
0 -2.4 TD
(On a 8x7 board, players alternate turns. On your turn you must either)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(move one of your pieces or pass your ball. The object is to get your)Tj
T*
(ball to your opponent's back line.)Tj
0 -3.6 TD
(      Initial board layout:)Tj
0 -2.4 TD
