0 -2.4 TD
(The Ohs player is attempting to move her ball \('O'\) to row 8. The Eks)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(player is attempting to move his ball \('X'\) to row 1. Ineligible)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(receivers are indicated by '~o~' and '~x~'.)Tj
0 -3.6 TD
(      Movement:)Tj
0 -2.4 TD
(Moves and passes must satisfy the following:)Tj
T*
(    * Pieces move like chess knights to any empty square.)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(    * The piece with the ball may not move.)Tj
T*
(    * The ball may be passed in a straight, unobstructed line to any of)Tj
T*
(      your pieces. The ball may be passed horizontally, vertically or)Tj
T*
(      diagonally.)Tj
T*
(    * You may pass the ball as many times as you like on a given turn so\)Tj
T*
(      long as no piece touches the ball more than once.)Tj
T*
(    * When a piece passes the ball, it becomes an ineligible receiver)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(      and may not receive further passes \(on later turns\). An ineligib\le)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(      receiver becomes eligible to receive passes after it moves.)Tj
T*
(    * If your opponent's previous move results in one of her pieces)Tj
T*
(      being adjacent to your ball, you must pass if you can. If you)Tj
T*
(      cannot pass, then you are free to move a piece. If one of your)Tj
T*
(      opponent's pieces is next to your ball, but it did not just move)Tj
T*
(      there, then it does not force you to pass.)Tj
T*
(    * You may not move so as to recreate an earlier board position.)Tj
0 -2.4 TD
